ption {:value "2006842"} "Half-Lightweight (≤66 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2006884"} "Lightweight (≤73 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2006926"} "Half-Middleweight (≤81 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2006968"} "Middleweight (≤90 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007010"} "Half-Heavyweight (≤100 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007052"} "Heavyweight (&gt;100 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007094"} "Extra-Lightweight (≤48 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007136"} "Half-Lightweight (≤52 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007220"} "Half-Middleweight (≤63 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007262"} "Middleweight (≤70 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007304"} "Half-Heavyweight (≤78 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007346"} "Heavyweight (&gt;78 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007388"} "Team, Mixed"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "900513"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "17405"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "18158"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "18896"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "19625"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "260689"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "316309"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "355006"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "18001298"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/352"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Lightweight (≤57 kilograms), Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "29 July 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2173"} "Grand Palais Éphémère, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2007178"} "28 from 28 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Canadian judokas " [:a {:href "/athletes/153216"} "Christa Deguchi"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101397"} "Jessica Klimkait"] " were world ranked #1 and #2 in this class as of June 2024 but, unfortunately, only one of them could compete in this class at Paris 2024. The Canadians chose Deguchi, who was World Champion in 2019 and 2023. Klimkait was a defending bronze medalist but she would not compete at Paris."] "\n\n" [:p {} "France pinned their hopes on " [:a {:href "/athletes/142750"} "Sarah-Léonie Cysique"] ", who had taken the silver medal in the class at Tokyo 2020 and won gold in the mixed team event, and also won three silvers at the Worlds since 2019. Kosovan " [:a {:href "/athletes/130985"} "Nora Gjakova"] " had won gold at Paris but, in a huge upset, she was defeated in round one by Mongolia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/153323"} "Lkhagvatogoogiin Enkhriilen"] ", with Gjakova ruled out for non-combativity after three " [:em {} "shidos"] " at 5:17, in extra time."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the quarter-finals, Deguchi had a first difficult match against " [:a {:href "/athletes/146582"} "Marica Perišić"] ", whom she defeated in extra time by " [:em {} "waza-ari"] ", at 4:29, despite receiving two " [:em {} "shidos"] " in the first three minutes of the fight. In the second quarter-finals match, Cysique had beaten Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/153289"} "Haruka Funakubo"] " by " [:em {} "ippon"] " in only eight seconds! Deguchi’s semi-final against Cysique was a huge and long fight. After 6:19, in extra time, the two women had two " [:em {} "shidos"] " and the fight was very indecisive. Finally, at 8:49, after video review by the referees, Cysique was disqualified for inserting her fingers inside Deguchi’s judogi. Cysique’s disqualification was very controversial and was written above extensively in French newspapers."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Deguchi finally took the gold medal by defeating Korea’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/153308"} "Heo Mi-Mi"] " in the final, after Heo was penalized in extra time at 6:35 for a third " [:em {} "shido"] " due to a false attack."] "\n\n" [:p {} "After her defeat in the semi-final, Cysique won a bronze medal by defeating Georgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/143212"} "Eteri Liparteliani"] ", using " [:em {} "sumi-otoshi"] " to win by " [:em {} "ippon"] " in 1:49. The other bronze medal went to Funakubo. She had lost to Heo in the semis but defeated Brazilian " [:a {:href "/athletes/122491"} "Rafaela Silva"] " to make the podium, after Silva was disqualified by " [:em {} "hansuko-make"] " at 9:06 in extra-time, for a forbidden “head dive” attack."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/153216"} "Christa Deguchi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/153308"} "Heo Mi-Mi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/153289"} "Haruka Funakubo"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:t